# Persistent memory

Your persistent memory lives at `$VAULT` (see `$VAULT/AGENTS.md` for full conventions).

## Quick rules

- **Read before writing.** At the start of a non-trivial session, run `/memory-load` (or shell out to `~/.copilot-memory/bin/memory-load`) before touching code.
- **Snapshot before ending.** When the user is wrapping up a session, run `/memory-save`.
- **Three-layer query rule** inside any project that has `graphify-out/`:
  1. Query `graphify-out/graph.json` or `graphify-out/wiki/index.md`
  2. Query the vault for decisions/progress
  3. Only read raw source files when editing
- **Zettelkasten** when writing vault notes:
  - Wikilinks (`[[note]]`), never markdown links for internal navigation
  - YAML frontmatter on every note (`title`, `tags`, `created`, `updated`, `status`, `type`)
  - kebab-case filenames
  - ≥ 2 wikilinks per permanent note

## Don't

- Don't re-read every file in the project to "orient yourself" — query the graph first
- Don't modify files inside `graphify-out/` manually
- Don't delete vault notes without asking
- Don't push git commits unless the user asks
